<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46788" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠίθεος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾔθεος</span></b>  (v.infr.), 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾄθεος</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Cerc.
			9.11
		</span></i>, but 
			Aeol.
		 (?) <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠΐθεος</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Sapph.
		</span></i> (v. infr.): ὁ:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unmarried youth</i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠίθεον ἢ καὶ γεγαμηκότα ἄπαιδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					877e
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				20a
			</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
				18
			</span></i> (pl.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένος ἠ. τε</span>
			joined, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				22.127
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χοροὺς παρθένων τε καὶ ἠιθέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.48
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Thes.</u>
				15
			</span></i>; including <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένοι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				B.
				16
			</span></i> tit., cf. <i><span class="en">
				43
			</span></i>, al.; of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωροί</span> sent to
			Delos, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				56.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ γάρ ἐστιν ᾔθεος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					945
				</span></i>
			; of animals, <i>unmated</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				840d
			</span></i>: later as Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παῖδες ἠίθεοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Thes.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠϊθέοισιν ἐφήβοισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					3.1151
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠίθεοι, οἱ</span>, <i>ghosts of those who die unmarried,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Tab.Defix.Aud.
				52.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> rare as
			fem., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠϊθέη</span>,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρθένος</span>, 
			<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				74.64
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.241
			</span></i> (Antip.&lt;Thess.&gt;); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόρη ᾔθεος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					332
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> metaph. as
				Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Marc.</u>
					33
				</span></i>
			. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠιθ-</span> shd. be read as
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾐθ-</span> in Prose.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
